{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Next Step"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Consent Forms Are Ready"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts. ."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le15ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Purpose Clauses: In order that, so that, for"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to explain the purpose or reason behind a decision or action, you can use purpose clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can introduce a purpose clause with:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">In order that</span> </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is important to be aware of the verbs and tenses when you use these phrases. <br/> Compare these two sentences:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She worked late in order / so as to <span class=\"strong\">complete </span>the work by the deadline.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"underline\">worked </span>late in order that /so that <span class=\"strong\">she <span class=\"underline\">could </span>complete the work by the deadline.</span></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"underline\">need </span>someone to present <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"strong\">so that we fill up </span></span>some time and people don't get bored. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've got an alternate entrance so that we don't clog up the main entrance."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had to research in order that I would know what the requirements of a consent form are."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll use it for getting permission to use photos."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need someone to present so that we fill up some time and people don't get bored. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you get him to come over here now so that we can go over what he's going to say?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Will to Express Willingness or Intention to do Something"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Will </span>and <span class=\"italic\">Would </span>are modals. You can use these modals to express willingness and intention. Willingness can be defined as the readiness to do something. Intention can be defined as an aim or plan."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">will </span>to express willingness."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I<span class=\"strong\">'ll </span>wash the plates if you put them away.</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">We're going to the museum. <span class=\"strong\">Will </span>you join us?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use will in the first person, it can express intention.<br/> For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ll </span>do my homework later tonight.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at some examples from the text:"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "consent form"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an official document confirming permission, approval, or agreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll take care of the consent forms. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about working conditions."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "requirement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a thing that is compulsory; a necessary condition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I had to research in order that I would know what the requirements of a consent form are."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "permission"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bact of \u200ballowing someone to do something, or of \u200ballowing something to \u200bhappen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll use it for getting permission to use photos."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "genre"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "categories or types"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He could come and speak about the genres of social media."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "engaging"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pleasant, interesting, and attractive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He's very engaging."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pertain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "be appropriate, related, or applicable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's important to understand how this information pertains to our project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you are a teacher at an elementary school. You and another teacher want to take your classes out on a field trip. The policy at the school requires consent forms from the students' parents."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Work with a classmate (you both are \u201cteachers\u201d) to create a consent form that is to be signed by your students' parents."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Internet to search for examples if you need help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include relevant information based on the field trip that you wish to take. For example, you can include information about when you will leave and come back, where you will go, safety concerns, and so on."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your consent form to another pair of students in your class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine the other pair of students are your students' parents."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the form to them and give reasons why you need to have them consent to this information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles and let the other pair present their consent form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the information on the consent form as a class when all groups are finished."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create a consent form for a field trip with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I include relevant information on the consent form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the consent form to another pair of classmates."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the consent form and listen to my classmates present their form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the information on the form as a class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can request or report about the purpose of events or actions related to job issues."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express willingness or intention to do something in work and job issues in a written way."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange complex professional information related to work and job issues."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some things that you might need to ask for consent for?"}, 